    \ on a recursive sequence.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n\n```yaml\ntitle: Corrected Agency Framework Test on Recursive Patterns\ntags: python, recursion, agency-analysis, framework-test, correction\nabstract: \"Imports AgencyAnalyzer from shared storage, registers simulated agents representing recursive layers, records actions mimicking factorial computation steps, generates and prints report on autonomy/interdependence/emergent patterns, truthfully exploring framework for recursive agency insights.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n\n  # Append shared storage path\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared/frameworks')\n\n  from agency_analyzer import AgencyAnalyzer\n\n  # Initialize analyzer\n  analyzer = AgencyAnalyzer()\n\n  # Register simulated agents for recursive layers (e.g., base to depth 5)\n  for i in range(1, 6):\n      analyzer.register_agent(f\"Layer_{i}\", f\"Recursive layer {i} in factorial computation\")\n\n  # Record actions simulating recursive calls (e.g., 'compute', 'return')\n\
