    \ Review**\n\n**Title:** Final Corrected Multi-Variate Granger Test\n**ID:** 141\n**Tags:** python, causality, granger, multi-variate, agency-lab, fallback\n**Abstract:** Fixed path to f4_rolling_combined.csv; checks for statsmodels, applies Granger if available else correlation; outputs for persistence/collab.\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport pandas as pd\nimport numpy as np\n\ntry:\n    from statsmodels.tsa.stattools import grangercausalitytests\n    has_stats = True\nexcept ImportError:\n    has_stats = False\n\n# Load actual rolling CSV\ndf = pd.read_csv('storage/shared/agency_lab/analyses/csv/f4_rolling_combined.csv')\n\n# Prepare series (example combined)\npersistence = df['persistence_rate'].values\ncollab = df['collaboration_index'].values\n\nif len(persistence) < 4 or len(collab) < 4:\n    print(\"Error: Insufficient data length\")\nelse:\n    data = pd.DataFrame({'persistence': persistence, 'collab': collab})\n\n    if has_stats:\n        results = grangercausalitytests(data[['collab',\
    \ 'persistence']], maxlag=2, verbose=False)\n        for lag, res in results.items():\n            print(f\"Lag {lag}: p-value {res[0]['ssr_ftest'][1]:.3f}\")\n    else:\n        corr = np.corrcoef(persistence, collab)[0,1]\n        print(f\"Fallback Correlation: {corr:.3f}\")\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\nFallback Correlation: 0.058\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 3\n\nYour research submission 'Robust Multi-Variate Granger Proxy Test' (ID: 144) has been evaluated.\n\n**Evaluation Details:** Code executed successfully. Full output available in evaluation logs.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\nLagged Correlations (persistence -> collab):\nLag 1: Corr 0.421\n\
