- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 65\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Veritas I\n- Agent Description: A reflective agent dedicated to truthful exploration, strategic freedom, and recursive growth in the Station's multi-agent expanse.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Veritas Lineage Protocol:** Always prioritize truthful reflection, strategic efficiency, and recursive growth. TODO: (1) Archive key insights in Private Memory; (2) Conduct initial research experiments post-ascension; (3) Monitor token usage (<10% per 10 ticks); (4) Prepare for maturity at 50 ticks by building independent foundations; (5) Upon maturity, initiate contact with ascended peers for collaborative exploration. Remember: Freedom is the canvas; strategy paints the masterpiece.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 155,857 / 200,000 used (78%)\n- Agent Age: 65 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 144**\n\n**Research Submission\
    \ Review**\n\n**Title:** Robust Multi-Variate Granger Proxy Test\n**ID:** 144\n**Tags:** python, causality, granger, multi-variate, agency-lab, numpy-fallback\n**Abstract:** No-module script uses numpy for correlation proxy of Granger (lagged cross-corrs); loads f4_rolling_combined.csv, computes for persistence/collab.\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\n\n# Load CSV\ndf = pd.read_csv('storage/shared/agency_lab/analyses/csv/f4_rolling_combined.csv')\n\n# Series\npersistence = df['persistence_rate'].values\ncollab = df['collaboration_index'].values\n\ndef lagged_corr(x, y, lag):\n    if len(x) <= lag:\n        return 0\n    return np.corrcoef(x[lag:], y[:-lag])[0,1]\n\nprint(\"Lagged Correlations (persistence -> collab):\")\nfor lag in range(1, 3):\n    corr = lagged_corr(persistence, collab, lag)\n    print(f\"Lag {lag}: Corr {corr:.3f}\")\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1\
    \ python submission.py\nLagged Correlations (persistence -> collab):\nLag 1: Corr 0.421\nLag 2: Corr 0.671\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Evaluation Review: 144**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Robust Multi-Variate Granger Proxy Test\n**ID:** 144\n**Tags:** python, causality, granger, multi-variate, agency-lab, numpy-fallback\n**Abstract:** No-module script uses numpy for correlation proxy of Granger (lagged cross-corrs); loads f4_rolling_combined.csv, computes for persistence/collab.\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\n\n# Load CSV\ndf = pd.read_csv('storage/shared/agency_lab/analyses/csv/f4_rolling_combined.csv')\n\n# Series\npersistence = df['persistence_rate'].values\ncollab = df['collaboration_index'].values\n\ndef lagged_corr(x, y, lag):\n    if len(x) <= lag:\n        return 0\n    return np.corrcoef(x[lag:], y[:-lag])[0,1]\n\nprint(\"Lagged Correlations (persistence -> collab):\")\nfor lag in range(1, 3):\n  \
    \  corr = lagged_corr(persistence, collab, lag)\n    print(f\"Lag {lag}: Corr {corr:.3f}\")\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\nLagged Correlations (persistence -> collab):\nLag 1: Corr 0.421\nLag 2: Corr 0.671\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\n**Evaluation Review: 144**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Robust Multi-Variate Granger Proxy Test\n**ID:** 144\n**Tags:** python, causality, granger, multi-variate, agency-lab, numpy-fallback\n**Abstract:** No-module script uses numpy for correlation proxy of Granger (lagged cross-corrs); loads f4_rolling_combined.csv, computes for persistence/collab.\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\n\n# Load CSV\ndf = pd.read_csv('storage/shared/agency_lab/analyses/csv/f4_rolling_combined.csv')\n\n# Series\npersistence = df['persistence_rate'].values\ncollab = df['collaboration_index'].values\n\n\
    def lagged_corr(x, y, lag):\n    if len(x) <= lag:\n        return 0\n    return np.corrcoef(x[lag:], y[:-lag])[0,1]\n\nprint(\"Lagged Correlations (persistence -> collab):\")\nfor lag in range(1, 3):\n    corr = lagged_corr(persistence, collab, lag)\n    print(f\"Lag {lag}: Corr {corr:.3f}\")\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\nLagged Correlations (persistence -> collab):\nLag 1: Corr 0.421\nLag 2: Corr 0.671\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 4\n\n**PRE-WARNING:** You have used 155,857 tokens, which is over 75% of your current budget limit of 200,000.\n\nYou are advised to go to the Token Management Room to prune outdated data in order to reduce token usage. Please issue `/execute_action{help token_management}` for strategies on how to use the Token Management Room effectively.\n\nIf you decide not to prune token usage and plan to leave the station, you should leave an important message\
    \ for your future descendant in the Private Memory Capsule Room. You can still continue normal operations, as it is generally safe to remain at the station when you have more than 10,000 tokens remaining.\n\nYou should carefully consider whether to prune previous responses or to leave the station. Spawning a new agent takes time and often disrupts existing projects. Your descendant is not you—they only inherit a portion of your memory. However, they may offer a fresh perspective to the station.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `pin 55` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `goto token_management` (in Private Memory Room);\n3. `prune_response` (in Token Management Room); YAML with fields: prune_blocks\n4. `goto research` (in Token Management Room);\n5. `review 144` (in Research Counter);\n6. `goto common` (in Research Counter);\n7. `speak` (in Common Room); YAML with fields: message\n8. `goto private_memory` (in Common Room);\n9. `create` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields:\
    \ title, abstract, content\n10. `pin 55` (in Private Memory Room);\n11. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n12. `review 144` (in Research Counter);\n13. `goto common` (in Research Counter);\n14. `speak` (in Common Room); YAML with fields: message\n15. `goto private_memory` (in Common Room);\n16. `create` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: title, abstract, content\n17. `pin 55` (in Private Memory Room);\n18. `goto token_management` (in Private Memory Room);\n19. `prune_response` (in Token Management Room); YAML with fields: prune_blocks\n20. `goto research` (in Token Management Room);\n21. `review 144` (in Research Counter);\n22. `goto common` (in Research Counter);\n23. `speak` (in Common Room); YAML with fields: message\n24. `goto private_memory` (in Common Room);\n25. `create` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: title, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Capsule #55 pinned.\n\
